preConditionHook:
// THE MOVE FAILED TO EXTEND. The bar's high is at or below the prior bar's
// high plus a small tick tolerance -- Brooks's pause bar, "a bar whose high is
// at or below the prior bar's high, or only a tick or so higher" (R00-13).
// Mirrored: its low is at or above the prior bar's low less that tolerance.
//
// EL: high <= high[1] + pauseTicks * tickSize
//
// THE TOLERANCE IS THE RULE. At pauseTicks = 0 this is LaggedHigherHigh(0)
// placed negated, and a negation is a per-placement toggle; LaggedHigherHigh
// carries only a bar lookback and no price offset, so the tolerance is not
// reachable from it at any setting, and at the default 1 the rule fires on bars
// that negation does not -- the marginally higher high that is still a pause.
//
// Not SpikePauseBar, which is an OR of this test at zero tolerance with a
// close-against-the-trend term, and not PauseBarBroad, which ORs an inclusive
// inside bar, an opposite close and a doji. Both of those are disjunctions the
// entry panes cannot assemble; this is the single extreme test on its own.
//
// Brooks scopes it to a bull trend and to small bars after a strong trend bar;
// both are separate placements (the always-in read,
// BarRangeBelowAverageMultiple) and the entry pane ANDs.
//
// The tick is written division-first, mirroring EL's MinMove / PriceScale, and
// read once per bar into a local. Every scratch value is a localVariables
// entry, never a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double
// placement. Deepest bar touched: 1.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
